<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch CPB updates macro forecasts for 1996, 1997.</title>
<headline>Dutch CPB updates macro forecasts for 1996, 1997.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch government's Central Planning Bureau (CPB) published the following updated forecasts for the Dutch economy on Wednesday:</p>
<p>					  1997	    1996	    1995</p>
<p>    Gross domestic product	2.75	    2.75 (2.5)    2.25</p>
<p>    Private consumption	   2.0  (1.75)   3.0  (2.5)    2.0</p>
<p>    Gross business investment   4.5  (2.5)    5.75 (4.5)   10.0</p>
<p>    Exports			   6.0	     4.25 (4.5)    8.75</p>
<p>    Imports			   5.75 (5.25)   4.5  (4.75)   8.25</p>
<p>    Consumer price index	  2.5	     2.0  (2.25)   2.0</p>
<p>NOTES - Figures in brackets show CPB forecasts published in September if these differ from updated forecasts.</p>
<p>All figures refer to real percentage changes versus previous year unless otherwise stated below.</p>
<p>CBS rounds off its estimates to nearest 0.25 percent. Gross business investment excludes housing. Exports exclude energy.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Kelly, Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
